The program for Linux in the scenario tree-choose: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/tree-choose.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Decided: CLAUDE.md, step 6
Why: the bell is a beep alone on Linux and on the web page, and moves nothing
(DEVIATIONS.md, L14; the user's word of 16 October 2026), where the bench's
BIOS moves the screen up a row for it with the cursor hidden below the last
row: from the beep at step 13 on, the screen keeps the panels' titles and the
key bar on its last row, a box that stands over the beep is drawn once, and
what the program draws later is on the rows it draws it at, where the
original's screen has it a row further up for every beep. The portable C's
patch of the scenario, of the key bar with Alt held, is not wanted here: that
bar is under the box of the tree, where the original's has gone up a row.

